              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Futura'>Average SDoH Risk Score</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Futura'>This metric provides a standardized measure of the social determinants of health (SDOH) risk across a population. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Futura'>It combines key social factors such as housing stability, internet access, educational attainment, demographic profiles, poverty, minority status, single-parent households, and unemployment rates into a single score. Each factor is assessed on a scale from 0 to 10, reflecting the extent of social risk they represent, with higher scores indicating higher risks. This composite score helps pinpoint regions where targeted social interventions could significantly enhance public health outcomes.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
