                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Futura'>This score represents the average risk based on medical conditions across all patients. Each medical condition is scored based on its potential impact on patient health and likelihood of readmission. Higher scores indicate a higher risk from medical conditions.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Futura'>Insights:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Futura'>- A higher Average Medical Score suggests a population with more severe health issues and a potentially higher need for medical intervention.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Futura'>- Use this score to prioritize areas for healthcare resource allocation and preventative care initiatives, such as Chronic Care Management RN services.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Futura'>Note: </run>
                <run fontname='Futura'>This score does not include readmission data. It is purely derived from existing medical diagnoses.</run>
              </formatted-text>
